WEBVTT

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.520
Simultaneous "leaving school" events.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.190
You're walking home from school with them?

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.400
I have my list of potential goddess hosts.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.860
All that's left is to get close to them.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.150
Is walking home with them really so important?

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.280
<b>Tomorrow's Forecast</b>

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.280
Amateur.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:17.710
Love means...

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.760
1) Walk home together!

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.430
<b>1) Walk home together</b>

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.310
<b>2) Exchange contact information</b>

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.190
2) Exchange contact information.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.170
3) Go on a date.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.100
<b>3) Go on a date</b>

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.810
<b>4) The girl invites you 
to walk home together!!</b>

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.770
4) The girl invites you to walk home together.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.820
Repeat 3 and 4!

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.440
<b>3) Go on a date</b>

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:26.940
<b>4) The girl invites you 
to walk home together!!</b>

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:27.440
<b>3) Go on a date</b>

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:27.980
<b>4) The girl invites you 
to walk home together!!</b>

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.800
The first step is walking home together!

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.790
If you can't get that part down,

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.980
you'll remain a novice in love forever.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.300
Stupid.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:36.720
Okay!

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.300
All done!

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.060
<b>(When not moon-watching) -> 13:00 Tsukiyo A <- Class Ends 

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.690
I'll follow this schedule.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.060
One hour for each of the five!

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.170
You can't do all that.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.020
Watch me.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.730
I'll raise my affection level with each girl by 5!

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.710
Is that a lot?

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.830
Okay, we'll stop there.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.650
Class is over.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.170
Enjoy your weekend.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:36.390
<i>It's raining?</i>

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:38.330
Ayumi!

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:39.770
'Sup, Chihiro?

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.110
Class is finally over...

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:45.180
Ah, Ayumi, Chihiro!

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:48.180
T-Time for band practice!

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.310
<b>Spell Makes Her 
Look Like This</b>

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.490
Hey, Ellie...

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:52.770
You're all fired-up.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:55.580
Right?

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.190
<b>Goddess Search, Day 3</b>

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.700
<i>Tsukiyo Kujo, from class 2-A, 
Astronomy Club President.</i>

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.170
<i>On that fateful night, I conquered Tsukiyo,</i>

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.060
<i>saving her from the loose soul,</i>

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.580
<i>and I figured her memory of that was gone.</i>

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.050
<i>So afterwards, I stayed away from her.</i>

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.280
<i>But...</i>

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:21.470
<i>I never want to see your face again!</i>

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.770
<i>Tsukiyo has memories of me, and she was angry.</i>

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.800
<i>In other words, it's very likely that 
a goddess is inside Tsukiyo.</i>

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.480
<i>Still...</i>

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.060
Why isn't she here?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.980
I'm already an hour behind schedule!

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.470
I hate the rain.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:42.040
Luna, are you wet?

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.620
H-Hey...

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.550
I waited for you so we could walk home together.

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:56.250
<i>She's a character who takes the bus to school?</i>

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.250
<i>What a pain!</i>

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.340
Let's go home together.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:02.760
Stay away from me,

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.720
you sick freak!

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.190
I need to make up for lost time...

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:08.580
What are you talking about?

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.380
Excuse me... We're leaving.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.280
<i>Clearing up what happened with 
Kanon should be simple,</i>

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.490
<i>but I want to keep things as they are for now.</i>

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.860
<i>In games, love triangles are standard.</i>

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.710
<i>Maintaining the triangle is easy enough.</i>

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.740
<i>The three F's that keep the triangle intact,</i>

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.250
<i>also known as Love's Delta Force!</i>

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.620
<i>First, you must quickly...</i>

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.120
<i>Follow!</i>

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:38.910
I don't know why there are all these 
rumors about Kanon and me.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.010
I would like you to stop talking to me.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.800
<i>Next...</i>

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.290
<i>Foolish!</i>

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:47.850
<i>A man must play the fool.</i>

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.480
My head!

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:53.390
Stupid.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.400
<i>And to seal the deal...</i>

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:01.120
<i>Finish with an open ending!</i>

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.150
<i>Avoid anything conclusive!</i>

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.790
<i>But I didn't have enough time to work with...</i>

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.210
<i>Her affection level hasn't...</i>

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.660
Use this.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:14.830
Th-Thanks.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.790
U-Uh, Tsukiyo?

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.410
I know tomorrow's Sunday,

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.130
but will you be in the astronomy club room?

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.630
If the night sky is clear.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:27.010
Yes!

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:28.590
Permission to enter!

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.220
<b>Light Music Club</b>

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.730
Wow, Ellie...

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:38.710
You've got your part down.

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:39.230
Yeah.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:40.990
You must have practiced hard.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:42.980
Oh, you think so?

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.210
That's a good girl.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.560
Should we call it a day?

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.680
Sounds good!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.200
Eh?

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:50.200
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.810
A warning from Haqua!

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.080
They've already finished practice?

00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:57.330
You're supposed to buy more time for me!

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:00.710
Well, ladies, I'm out.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.130
You count as a lady.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:03.750
Bye-bye!

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:06.220
<i>Yui left!</i>

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.880
<i>I h-have to stop the other two!</i>

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.970
Um, why don't we talk for a bit?

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:15.390
Oh, Ellie... Did you need something?

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.760
I got a call from Katsuragi last night.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:20.900
From Katsuragi?

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:22.870
Uh-huh.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.780
Hmm?

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.940
Oh, then I'm leaving.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:27.860
Sure.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.120
So what did you want?

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.330
I'm off to a bad start...

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:38.850
Yui...

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:40.080
Crap, she's about to leave.

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:41.580
I'll run into the car if need be!

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:51.030
A very inconvenient turn of events.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.230
Doesn't anyone care what happens to Kanon?

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:54.120
Katsuragi?

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:56.990
<i>Ayumi?</i>

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:58.700
<b>Tsukiyo 

00:06:58.700 --> 00:06:58.870
<b>Tsukiyo 

00:06:58.870 --> 00:06:59.080
<b>Tsukiyo 

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.440
<b>Tsukiyo 

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:01.440
<i>Adjust!</i>

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.570
I waited for you so we could walk home together.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:08.440
What are you doing, Katsuragi?

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:13.960
<i>Screw the real world!</i>

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.850
<i>The walk home from school is a critical 
chance to increase affection level!</i>

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.080
It stopped raining.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:18.080
<i>So...</i>

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.460
<i>Why is Miyako here?</i>

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.450
Yeah.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:23.140
<i>In games, walking home together 
is pointless when you're not alone!</i>

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.030
<b>U-Um... Let's walk home together?</b>

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:27.070
<b>Is... Is that okay...?</b>

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:26.850
<i>In games, only little sisters and 
childhood friends can interfere!</i>

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:28.340
<i>Wait...</i>

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.100
<i>I have no time...</i>

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.680
<i>Ignore Miyako, and proceed with the plan.</i>

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.510
Ayumi, how did you do on the last test?

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:38.880
I'd guess that you—

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.630
Hey, Katsuragi...

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:44.020
If you walk home with us, 
won't Kanon be mad?

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.150
<i>That was unnecessary.</i>

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:49.790
Yeah, I never would've expected 
Katsuragi and Kanon as a couple.

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:52.910
When did that happen?

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:55.560
Oh! I wanna hear the story!

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.010
<i>Please, Miyako, cut me some slack!</i>

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:01.660
<i>Her affection level is dropping...</i>

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.120
<i>Time to recover.</i>

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:06.130
It's just a rumor.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.470
The truth is that...

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:12.630
<i>Haqua and Chihiro?!</i>

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.010
<i>Why are they here?</i>

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:17.700
Oh, I'm dying for some of the taiyaki here!

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:15.140
Huh?

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.660
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.230
What's this about?

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.220
Let's go inside!

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:20.340
No!

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:27.770
<i>They came in!</i>

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:30.280
Should we check the usual music store?

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:32.690
So, the second floor?

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:34.360
Y-Yes!

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:37.330
Katsuragi?

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.470
Katsuragi, you wanted ogura, right?

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.500
Y-Yeah...

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:44.840
It's hot, so I'll wrap another napkin around it.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:45.790
Here!

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:50.070
No point being nice to me now.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.570
If a loose soul gets inside you, I won't help.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:53.640
Huh?

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.110
Hey, where are you going?

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:56.180
The restroom!

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:58.300
Eat that first...

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.820
Haqua...

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:09.010
Chihiro said she wanted to visit the music shop.

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:11.290
They all just have to do things their own way...

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:13.190
Do your job right!

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:15.230
You do realize how important 
these conquests are?

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:16.320
I know!

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:19.160
Katsuragi!

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.330
Ayumi...

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:24.140
Were you just talking to someone?

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:25.570
No one...

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:27.170
Uh, did you need something?

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.290
Y-Yeah...

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:37.520
I d-don't have time to waste on you...

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:40.930
So don't talk to me anymore!

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.310
Got it?

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:43.350
I refuse.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:46.190
I will continue to follow you around!

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:49.420
Let me go—

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:53.530
Sorry, but you can't say anything to stop me.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.140
Ayumi!

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:07.170
What are you doing here?

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:08.330
E-Ellie...

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:11.340
Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.340
<b>Kurokawa Music</b>

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:14.450
Ellie's taking a long time in the restroom...

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:16.430
Does she have a stomachache or something?

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:19.850
Katsuragi?

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:20.840
What are you doing?

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:22.400
Oh, Chihiro.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.850
Elsie asked me to pick up some bass strings.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.200
But I can't tell which to get.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.360
Where's Ellie?

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.140
Something came up, so she left.

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:31.900
Eh?!

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.800
I'm guessing she wants these.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:38.030
What's the difference?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.900
The thickness is different.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.120
Thickness?

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.540
Is there any need for so many 
different guitars, anyway?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:45.850
Aren't they all the same?

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:47.740
Idiot, they're all different.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:48.620
How so?

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.430
I don't know!

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:52.780
You don't?

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:55.320
Well, I'm still a beginner.

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.380
I've only been playing guitar for six months.

00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:00.450
Wow, this one's amazing!

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:01.630
What's with that price?

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:03.260
Think how many games you could buy.

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:07.070
Excuse me!

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.640
Oh, Katsuragi... Stand near me.

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:18.650
Or it's too embarrassing.

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:42.050
Well? Did the expensive one sound better?

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.890
I couldn't even tell.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:45.050
I was too nervous...

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:47.960
What was that song you were singing?

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:49.060
Oh, that?

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:51.860
It's a song I wrote.

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:52.560
You wrote it?

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:55.560
The plan is to perform an original 
song for the Mai High Festival,

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.120
but I've only finished the beginning.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:11:59.790
Really?

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:01.070
But...

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:07.080
It sounded pretty nice.

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:11.930
You can't judge a song by the beginning—

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.130
Why am I talking to you about this?!

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:19.300
That's just weird...

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:26.740
<i>I'm making progress with Ayumi and Chihiro.</i>

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:28.470
Oh, Ellie...

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:30.620
Pay for your brother's taiyaki.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.010
Huh?!

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.730
Next up is Shiori.

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:42.610
<b>Closed for Today</b>

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:40.740
The library's closed...

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:42.610
That makes my job easier.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.390
Sorry.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.740
<b>Shiori</b>

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:29.530
<i>"The lingering light particles 
from the bombardment</i>

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:31.810
<i>gathered into concentrated lasers,</i>

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:35.320
<i>until space was filled with light beams 
large enough to blow up planets.</i>

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:38.230
<i>Stardate 20 DA.</i>

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:43.330
<i>The Ancestor Galactic War has been 
raging for six hundred years."</i>

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.500
"My name is Simone...

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.400
Simone S. Libro!

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.640
I've become a galactic reporter, 
and it's like a dream come true!"

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.840
<i>SF? Plus a galactic war?</i>

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:56.770
<i>This will spin out of control...</i>

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:00.610
I-Is someone there?

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:02.540
"Editor-in-Chief!

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:06.790
We have a responsibility to denounce 
the crimes committed in this war.

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:08.480
Why is there an article on space dumplings?"

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:09.590
"Shut up!

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:11.280
You're fired!"

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:14.830
<i>"As punishment, I have to 
sort articles every day.</i>

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.970
<i>I never get to go into space..."</i>

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:21.290
"I have a bad habit of saying 
everything that comes to mind.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.730
I wish I could learn to keep my mouth shut.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:25.960
It'll never happen."

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:27.440
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.590
<i>The main character is the 
author's total opposite...</i>

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:33.100
<i>"In the library, I met a strange man.</i>

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.370
<i>His name is Kashiragi.</i>

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:36.480
<i>Pierre Kashiragi."</i>

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:38.410
"Books are wonderful.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:40.350
They contain the human race's legacy."

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:42.860
"Books are a relic of the past."

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:44.480
<i>Kashiragi?</i>

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.900
"Don't write in the books."

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:48.740
"I was making corrections."

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:51.490
"We seem to be talking a lot."

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.370
"Are we friends now?"

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:57.620
"Simone, you're like a main character."

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:00.120
"Don't say stuff like that."

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:03.320
<i>The roles are reversed, but this 
is how my conquest went.</i>

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:07.060
<i>Then, Shiori remembers the conquest.</i>

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:11.040
"I'm too scared to go into space."

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:15.730
"Very well.

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:17.060
I'll give you the courage."

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.720
<i>This is how my conquest went!</i>

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:20.070
<i>Which means, after this...</i>

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:22.770
<i>Huh? There's nothing written down.</i>

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.760
"Kashiragi died."

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:29.570
<i>Eh?!</i>

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.190
<i>"Kashiragi was shot and killed in battle.</i>

00:15:33.190 --> 00:15:35.990
<i>I held a space funeral for Kashiragi."</i>

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:38.500
<i>Kashiragi! Why are you suddenly dead?!</i>

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.900
<i>"I didn't feel bad at all."</i>

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:43.710
<i>Her attitude completely changed.</i>

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:47.480
<i>Is this because of the Kanon rumors?</i>

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:56.340
Uh...

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.350
You shouldn't...

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:04.100
<i>She can't become Simone.</i>

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:05.500
Sorry.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:09.530
I added something to the end.

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:11.030
The end?

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:14.570
<i>"A few days later, the capsule returned."</i>

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:17.840
"I didn't die!

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:20.700
Thanks to my space body armor, 
I escaped without a scratch!"

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.440
"No one told you to come back to life!

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:36.300
And don't add stupid plot devices!"

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:41.430
"I just wanted to see you again."

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:47.280
<i>"Kashiragi was swallowed whole 
by a vicious Renbatos and died!</i>

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:48.570
<i>I wasn't sad at all."</i>

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:51.600
<i>"Kashiragi was never digested and escaped.</i>

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:53.320
<i>It was a miracle."</i>

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:55.440
"Why do you keep coming back to life?

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:57.610
I don't want to see you!

00:16:57.610 --> 00:17:00.080
And Kashiragi isn't supposed to talk so much!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:03.560
Besides, I have a story on nebula 
synthetic negi ramen

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.330
I need to work on..."

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:09.840
<b>Don't be mad at me, Simone.</b>

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:13.800
"I want to spend more time with you.

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:18.050
Can I help you with your 
story on nebula ramen?"

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:31.670
<b>To be continued.</b>

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.770
<i>Well, that's enough for now.</i>

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:41.930
Um...

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:47.150
It's "nebula synthetic negi ramen."

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.320
Okay...

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.170
The story will continue.

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:55.330
But my goal is to trigger 
a "leaving school" event.

00:17:55.730 --> 00:17:56.550
Haqua...

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:58.790
Watch from above,

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:00.630
and tell me when Shiori leaves.

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:02.580
I'll accidentally run into her.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:03.930
Fine.

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:06.560
So stupid.

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:07.110
No one's inside...

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:08.520
Where'd he go?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:09.510
Yui!

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:11.520
Hey...

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:12.450
Why are you here?!

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:13.900
I saw you take a car home!

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:16.530
I wanted to walk home with you.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.910
I spotted you from the car.

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:23.130
These days, it isn't safe outside,

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:26.770
so I couldn't let a helpless 
boy walk home alone.

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:27.750
Hold on...

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:29.090
That's what boys say to girls.

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.170
You come later...

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:31.670
Don't trigger events on your own!

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:33.420
<i>What's with her?</i>

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:34.900
<b>Let's walk home together.</b>

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:36.960
<i>She's acting more like a playable 
character than a heroine.</i>

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:39.470
<i>Which means that I'm her target.</i>

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:41.420
<i>Player versus player?</i>

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:42.740
<i>That takes courage!</i>

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:46.260
I don't need you to walk me home.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.810
I'm a man, so I should walk you home.

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:52.820
That made my heart skip...

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:55.680
Every now and then, 
you have this nice expression...

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:56.570
<i>Good.</i>

00:18:56.970 --> 00:19:01.820
But earlier, you used the same 
look on Ayumi and Chihiro.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:03.150
<i>What?!</i>

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:05.120
I was watching you.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:07.830
I didn't think you were a playboy...

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.160
<i>Playboy?</i>

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:11.510
Here's a present!

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:15.390
<i>There are too many new elements!</i>

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:17.070
<i>I can't process everything!</i>

00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:18.170
It's an item you'll definitely need in the future...

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:20.660
A girl's Mai High uniform!

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:23.060
The hell am I supposed to do with this?!

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:25.060
Obviously, you're going to wear it.

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:29.600
It would look strange if both members 
of a couple wore male uniforms.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.940
Why don't you dress like a girl?!

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:33.440
You'll get used to it soon enough.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.600
I don't want to get used to it!

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:36.690
And we're not a couple!

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:37.780
Is this a comedy act?

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:41.590
I realize that you may be a bad person.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:45.630
But I will teach you true love!

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:47.830
It's not true love if we're both cross-dressing!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.490
Don't worry...

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:51.460
Love will overcome all.

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:56.460
Shiori?

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:57.210
Now!

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:00.280
Haqua...

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:01.760
Honestly...

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:03.720
I was scared!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.760
Let's go home!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.030
Yeah, yeah.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.600
<b>Goddess Search, Day 4</b>

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.600
<i>Today, we caught Kanon after a recording session</i>

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.100
<i>for an interview!</i>

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:16.820
<i>We asked her about the juicy 
rumors floating around!</i>

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:16.820
<i>I managed to trigger "leaving school" events, 
but it's going slowly.</i>

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:21.610
<i>If their affection drops to hate, the conquest 
will take too long or it's game over.</i>

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:28.740
<b>Ayumi            Shiori             Yui             Tsukiyo        Chihiro</b>

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.990
<i>I estimate these are the current affection levels.</i>

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:28.360
<i>I should start by spending Sunday with...</i>

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:32.600
Guess I'll go see all of them.

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:33.960
Hi!

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:38.500
Long time, no see.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:40.660
Why is Nora here?

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:41.430
Does she know about Kanon?

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:42.320
No way!

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:43.630
Either way, she's trouble.

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:47.050
She once tried to kill me!

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:49.220
She's a co-worker!

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:50.930
She wouldn't go that far...

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:51.940
Probably.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:54.510
Hey, don't ignore me!

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:55.700
Is Elsie around?

00:20:56.470 --> 00:20:57.230
Haqua?

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:58.600
Why are you here?

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:00.500
I'm j-just visiting...

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.280
What brings you here?

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:04.740
Just a message to pass along.

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:07.080
So, where's Elsie?

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:08.850
I don't think she's around.

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:11.630
Oh, tough luck...

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:12.410
Listen to me.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:15.050
Don't let her find Kanon.

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:16.370
I know that!

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:23.880
You're more useful than my stupid Buddy.

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:27.110
I'm glad that you like me!

00:21:27.110 --> 00:21:28.640
Eh? What was that?

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:31.500
Why are you sucking up to her?

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:32.870
I changed my mind.

00:21:32.870 --> 00:21:34.580
Ask her for information.

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:36.020
I s-see...

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:37.930
Hey, Nora?

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:39.370
Why do you need to talk to Elsie?

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:44.280
We have new orders from the bureau.

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:48.780
We're supposed to find residents of 
Heaven who are hiding on Earth.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:51.650
I didn't hear anything about that!

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:53.470
This is still confidential.

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:55.460
The official announcement will be tomorrow.

00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:57.730
They're talking about the goddesses, right?

00:21:57.730 --> 00:21:58.540
That means...

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:00.840
What are goddesses?

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:03.700
You just worry about catching loose souls!

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:05.920
Man, stop irritating me...

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:07.610
Haqua...

00:22:08.780 --> 00:22:10.620
I'm going to the library.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:14.630
I need you to maintain relations with Nora 
so we can squeeze information out of her.

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:15.560
Huh?

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:17.370
M-Maintain relations?

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:18.310
Wait!

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:24.650
<i>More support for my theory that all 
the goddesses are in this city.</i>

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:27.520
<i>Kanon will only last a few more days.</i>

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:31.780
<i>But my conquests aren't 
proceeding as planned...</i>

00:22:32.140 --> 00:22:33.410
<i>I have to hurry!</i>

00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:07.840
Tsukiyo, Shiori, Yui, Ayumi, Chihiro...

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:09.880
This school is full of potential goddesses.

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:11.320
If this were a game,

00:24:11.320 --> 00:24:13.600
some secret would explain the coincidence.

00:24:13.600 --> 00:24:15.300
I want to help!

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:17.580
You'd better not be the last goddess...

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:18.830
Ah! A fire engine!

00:24:18.830 --> 00:24:20.270
You aren't, right?!
